["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-5378569c7b2da26b1ef6f17891b53e79282f5755ffe2cf9fe0d2b88ddb50de44","command_type":"aep.entity.update/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-body","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"changes":{"body":"## Context\n\nImplements the format `story:graph-projection-specification` declares, in a new workspace crate `ekr-views` (roadmap § 3 names it for rendered views and query scopes). This is the Rust that `ekr view` serves and that later rendered views (§ 82) build on.\n\nDesign sections served: § 82 (deterministic projection; every fact carries its assertion id), § 47 (scope: canonical as of revision N), § 95 (schema lineage), § 62 (ids that reach the explain chain). Epic exit criterion: two renders of the same revision are byte-identical.\n\n## What to build\n\n- Crate `crates/ekr-views`, added to the workspace, with ESS domain `ekr.views` as its declaration. It names no domain concept.\n- A render function from a committed revision to the bytes of `ekr.graph-projection/1`. The canonical state comes from the kernel read surface (`Runtime::snapshot` / `Runtime::replay`), the schema history from each revision's ontology, evidence retention from `Runtime::content`. Prefer a pure function over already-loaded snapshots with the loading beside it, so determinism is a property of the pure part.\n- Reads only. No propose, validate or commit path is reachable from this crate's public API.\n- The `ekr-views` conformance suite from the specification story runs against this renderer through the real kernel on both providers, in the shape `crates/ekr/tests/conformance.rs` and `task conform-check` already use for `ekr-kernel`.\n\nWatch: schema history replays every revision up to the projected one; `task:selected-revision-loads-read-one-event-per-call` (draft) says those loads are slow. Measure on a store of a few hundred revisions and report it; do not fix the store here.\n\n## Domain relations\n\nRests on every relation listed in `story:graph-projection-specification` § Domain relations, with the citations given there. The ones this crate reads directly:\n\n- `Assertion → subject` — inferable (**inferred** from `crates/ekr-graph/src/assertion.rs:39`; no ess/1 relation declares it).\n- `Revision → SchemaVersion` — inferable (**inferred** from `crates/ekr-graph/src/canonical.rs:446` and `crates/ekr-kernel/src/runtime.rs:233`; no ess/1 relation declares it).\n- `Evidence → retained bytes` — inferable (**inferred** from `crates/ekr-kernel/src/runtime.rs:253`; no ess/1 relation declares it).\n- `Assertion → Support → Evidence` — `systems/ekr/domains/graph.yaml`, `ekr.graph.Assertion` relation `support`, `ekr.graph.Support` relation `evidence`.\n\nNot assumed: `decision-blocker:relation-assertion-edge-correspondence`. Relation assertions stay on their subject node; Edges stay Edges.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nHTTP, the viewer, role derivation, templates, other query scopes.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nOn each of the file and SQLite providers, a test renders one revision of a seeded, schema-evolved fixture store twice in one process and once more in a fresh process after reopening, and the three renders are byte-identical and pass the committed `ekr-views` conformance suite with no skipped or unsupported scenario.\n"},"command":"update-entity","target":"ent-eb40f8e03602724c0b253f5d1682cbbd"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-eb40f8e03602724c0b253f5d1682cbbd@3"],"audit":["aud-f96a0cb6de8f81692ecff75430880516"],"command_id":"cmd-child-5378569c7b2da26b1ef6f17891b53e79282f5755ffe2cf9fe0d2b88ddb50de44","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-f96a09b6de8f7c502ecff65430880363"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"agent:claude-decomposer-p4-operator-surface","causation":"cmd-child-5378569c7b2da26b1ef6f17891b53e79282f5755ffe2cf9fe0d2b